fact WorkItem(id: "WI-279", description: some(value: "Dot dispatch as a CLIENT of the type-directed [simp] engine (WI-283). See docs/design/simp-dot-finding.md. A dot rule is the same shape as a spec/sort equational rule — sort-scoped, requires-guarded (e.g. a custom Either.map: dot(?e,map,[?f])=either_map(?e,?f) :- requires Either; concrete RHS) — selected by min_sort(receiver) = widen the receiver to its least declared sort (= sort_head(TypeResult.ty); sort_functor_of extracts it; a compile-time typer notion, never a goal, never a runtime/callable typeof). Firing reuses the engine's tree-producing walk (DotApply -> Apply, rebuild ancestors, write the body back — type_check_node only types, so dot NEEDS the walk) and runs IN the typer (scope-correct min_sort). Beyond sort-specific rules there is an engine DEFAULT fallback (resolve name to an op on min_sort(receiver), or a field on a free-standing entity -> field_access) — engine logic, NOT a writable rule (functor dynamically resolved). Produced Apply rides normal type-param inference + req_insertion (043 6.6). Reverted predecessor (this session) ran a standalone PRE-typer pass with a reconstructed flat op-level env (build_op_env) — wrong: typer-independent, omits let/lambda/match scope. DEPENDS ON WI-283. Acceptance: ?x.method(args)/?x.field dispatch via receiver sort with no import; a sort-specific requires-guarded dot rule (Either-style) overrides the default; receivers referencing let/lambda/match-bound locals dispatch; clear no-match error at the dot span; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-283"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-14T16:24:04Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-279", author: "user", content: "=== IMPLEMENTATION PLAN + EXPLORATION (self-contained; re-claimed 2026-05-29, fresh deep-read) ===\n\nDESIGN (settled, docs/design/simp-dot-finding.md): the [simp] engine is type-directed and runs IN the typer. Dot dispatch is one of its clients. typeof is NOT a goal — it is min_sort (widen receiver to its least declared sort = sort_head(TypeResult.ty); sort_functor_of extracts it, typing.rs:7859). The DEFAULT fallback (resolve name to an op on min_sort(receiver), or a field on a free-standing entity) is ENGINE LOGIC, not a writable rule. Sort-specific dot rules ARE [simp] rules of shape dot_apply(?e, name, args)=RHS guarded by the enclosing sort requires; they OVERRIDE the default.\n\nKEY DECISION: dedicated typer arm, NOT the generic matcher. Reason: the generic [simp] matcher cannot see DotApply — occ_head (term_view.rs:74-104) maps DotApply to ViewHead::Opaque, and try_fire (simp_rewrite.rs:256-260) only fires on Expr::Apply/Constructor functors (returns None for DotApply). So dot dispatch is handled directly in visit_type.\n\nHOOK POINT: Expr::DotApply currently falls into the BottomExpr error arm at typing.rs:1492 (visit_type). Replace with a real arm. Mirror the Expr::Apply machinery: visit_type Apply arm (typing.rs:1367-1387), TypeBuildFrame::Apply (enum ~typing.rs:938), build_type Apply arm (typing.rs:1602-1645, with the fire->re-Visit pattern at 1630-1635).\n\nPLUMBING:\n[A] visit_type Expr::DotApply{receiver,name,pos_args,named_args}: push TypeBuildFrame::DotApply{occ,name,env,expected,fuel}, then child Visits in reverse (named, pos, receiver) so receiver pops first. receiver typed with no hint; args no hint.\n[B] add TypeBuildFrame::DotApply variant.\n[C] build_type DotApply arm: drain child results [receiver,...pos,...named]; collect_arg_errors -> propagate Err; reassemble (DotApply has a reassemble arm already, simp_rewrite.rs:503; is_rewritable already admits DotApply, simp_rewrite.rs:202). Then resolve+synthesize (below). On success push_visit(synth_apply, env, expected, fuel-1) and RETURN (re-types the synthesized Apply, riding normal Apply typing + type-param inference + req_insertion 043 6.6). On no-match -> Err(no-match diagnostic at the dot span). On unresolved receiver type (min_sort None) -> same no-match/undecidable error at dot span.\n\nRESOLUTION ORDER in the build arm:\n1. min_sort = sort_functor_of(receiver_result.ty)  (use the child result.ty directly; do not rely on inferred_type stamping which happens in the separate Stamp frame).\n2. (INCREMENT 2) sort-specific dot rule: a [simp]-tagged equation whose LHS is dot_apply(receiver-pattern, name-literal, args) scoped to a sort the receiver min_sort satisfies. OVERRIDES default. Needs: (a) occ_head DotApply->Functor{dot_apply,[receiver, name, ...args]} arm (term_view.rs:71 anticipates a dot_apply functor; convert.rs:1248-1266 already builds the term shape dot_apply(receiver, Ident(name), ...pos, ...named)) + broaden try_fire (simp_rewrite.rs:256-260) to accept DotApply; (b) a DOT-AWARE guard — simp_fire_guard_holds (typing.rs:7922) is for spec-op functors (lookup_spec_op_dispatch), NOT dot_apply; a dot rule guard = receiver min_sort provides the rule enclosing sort (reuse sort_provides, typing.rs:8664). Simplest integration: in the dedicated arm try fire_simp on the DotApply node FIRST (after the occ_head/try_fire broadening + dot guard), and only fall to the default if nothing fired.\n3. DEFAULT fallback method: find_operation_in_scope(kb, receiver_sort_ref_term, name_short) (load.rs:3093) -> op_sym. Synthesize Apply(op_sym, pos=[receiver_node, ...pos_arg_nodes], named=[...]) so x.m(a) becomes m(x,a). NOTE this is OPS-DECLARED-ON-THE-SORT, NOT spec-satisfaction (Int provides Ordered): sort_ops_lookup(Int,min)=None per WI-281; spec-satisfaction dot dispatch is WI-281 (blocked on this), so out of scope here.\n4. DEFAULT fallback field (zero-arg DotApply, name is a field on a free-standing-entity receiver): synthesize field access. OPEN: field-access IR repr is NOT a field_access symbol in typing.rs/node_occurrence.rs — investigate how a field read is represented post-dispatch (Apply to a field accessor? reflect op? entity_field_types). Lower priority than the method case.\n\nSYNTHESIS API: NodeOccurrence::synthesized_expr(Expr::Apply{functor,pos_args,named_args,type_args:Vec::new()}, Rc::clone(&dot_occ), pass, dot_occ.owner) (pattern at simp_rewrite.rs:357-362). pass: reuse simp_pass(kb) or add a dot PassId.\n\nWHY DEDICATED ARM / IN THE TYPER (the reverted-WI-278 lesson): the reverted predecessor ran a standalone PRE-typer pass with a reconstructed flat op-level env (build_op_env) — wrong, because it was typer-independent and omitted let/lambda/match scope. Running in visit_type means env carries the full lexical scope, so receivers referencing let/lambda/match-bound locals resolve (acceptance item 3, free). (build_op_env code is NOT in the tree — only referenced in a docs commit; nothing to clean.)\n\nINCREMENTS (land green slices; deliver only when all acceptance met):\n- INC 1 (method default fallback): items 1 (no-import dispatch via receiver sort), 3 (let/lambda/match receivers), 4 (no-match error at dot span). The bounded core.\n- INC 1b: field default fallback (resolve the field-access repr first).\n- INC 2: sort-specific requires-guarded dot rule overrides default (item 2) — needs occ_head dot_apply arm + try_fire broadening + dot-aware guard.\n\nTEST GATE: full anthill-core (typing_test, parse_tests stdlib, wi_tests). Add: x.method(args) dispatch with no import; let/lambda/match-bound receiver dispatches; clear no-match error at the dot span; (INC 2) Either-style sort-specific dot rule overrides the default. Eval currently errors on any surviving DotApply (eval.rs:198 + typing.rs comment) — once dispatch rewrites them, runnable.\n\nAPI REFS: sort_functor_of typing.rs:7859; min_sort 7892; find_operation_in_scope load.rs:3093; sort_ops_lookup mod.rs:1373 (WI-281, not 279); NodeOccurrence::synthesized_expr simp_rewrite.rs:357; reassemble DotApply arm simp_rewrite.rs:503; is_rewritable DotApply simp_rewrite.rs:202; try_fire/occ_head bail simp_rewrite.rs:256-260 + term_view.rs:74-104; simp_fire_guard_holds typing.rs:7922; sort_provides typing.rs:8664; convert dot_apply term shape convert.rs:1248-1266; apply_eq_rules runtime deliberately skips type-directed rules (resolve.rs:1453-1465) — dot is typer-only.\n\nSTATUS: re-claimed; deep-read complete; NO code landed yet (a sizable typer feature; per the WI history, not started at a long session tail). Next session: implement INC 1 against this plan.", at: "2026-05-29T19:40:08Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-279", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-14 (commit 3f20427). INC1b (?x.field constructor-field access) — the final acceptance item — landed; INC1/INC2 already on main. Typer (build_type DotApply arm): a zero-arg ?x.field that matches no operation resolves member->field by SHORT name (use-site intern != declaring entity's field symbol), projects the field type via resolve_field_type (substitutes receiver type-args, same path pattern field types use), and synthesizes field_access(receiver, \"field\") = the reflect field-access desugaring; result type set directly + inferred_type stamped (no field-specific signature to re-type against); method fallback runs first so an op shadows a same-named field. Eval: new Value-level anthill.reflect.field_access builtin (runtime twin of the SLD BuiltinTag::FieldAccess) reads Value::Entity.named by short name. ALSO surfaced+fixed eval-runnability of the ?x value-receiver dot forms: a value-receiver ?x reaches eval as Expr::Var(Global) (the only op-body var not already Ref/VarRef), which eval's Var arm rejected outright — now Global resolves by name; DeBruijn (unopened param) + Rigid (skolem type-param) stay loud errors. So BOTH ?x.method and ?x.field are now runnable (prior INC1/INC2 tests only type-checked, never evaluated a ?x receiver). Tests: field type+eval (concrete + generic Option substitution), field no-match, e2e ?b.total(10)+?b.value method-and-field eval. Full anthill-core 1470/0 green. /code-review (2 finders): fixed Var::Rigid unsound-resolution (kept loud) + stamped synth inferred_type; effects=recv.effects confirmed correct (receiver sub-expr evaluated, effects propagate).", at: "2026-06-14T16:23:58Z")
